    "Data structures and interfaces": "classDiagram\n    class Position {\n        +Position(int x, int y)\n        +int getX()\n        +int getY()\n        +Position translate(int dx, int dy)\n        +boolean equals(Object o)\n        +int hashCode()\n    }\n    enum Orientation {\n        NORTH, EAST, SOUTH, WEST\n        +int dx()\n        +int dy()\n        +Orientation left()\n        +Orientation right()\n    }\n    enum Command {\n        MOVE_FORWARD, TURN_LEFT, TURN_RIGHT, FIRE\n    }\n    class Tank {\n        -String id\n        -Position position\n        -Orientation orientation\n        -int health\n        +Tank(String id, Position position, Orientation orientation, int health)\n        +String getId()\n        +Position getPosition()\n        +Orientation getOrientation()\n        +int getHealth()\n        +boolean isAlive()\n        ~void setPosition(Position position)\n        ~void rotateLeft()\n        ~void rotateRight()\n        ~void applyDamage(int amount)\n        +Tank copy()\n    }\n    class Projectile {\n        -String shooterId\n        -Position position\n        -Orientation orientation\n        +Projectile(String shooterId, Position position, Orientation orientation)\n        +String getShooterId()\n        +Position getPosition()\n        +Orientation getOrientation()\n        ~void setPosition(Position position)\n        +Projectile copy()\n    }\n    class ObstacleMap {\n        +static ObstacleMap empty()\n        +void add(Position p)\n        +boolean isBlocked(Position p)\n        +ObstacleMap copy()\n    }\n    class Arena {\n        -int width\n        -int height\n        -ObstacleMap obstacles\n        +Arena(int width, int height, ObstacleMap obstacles)\n        +boolean inBounds(Position p)\n        +boolean isObstacle(Position p)\n        +Arena copy()\n    }\n    class ScoreBoard {\n        -Map~String,Integer~ hits\n        -Map~String,Integer~ kills\n        +ScoreBoard(Collection~String~ ids)\n        +void addHit(String id)\n        +void addKill(String id)\n        +int getHits(String id)\n        +int getKills(String id)\n        +int getScore(String id)\n        +Map~String,Integer~ asMap()\n        +ScoreBoard copy()\n        +void reset(Collection~String~ tankIds)\n    }\n    class GameEngine {\n        -Arena arena\n        -final Arena initialArena\n        -Map~String,Tank~ tanks\n        -final Map~String,Tank~ initialTanks\n        -final ScoreBoard scoreBoard\n        +GameEngine(Arena arena, List~Tank~ tanks)\n        +void enqueue(String tankId, Command cmd)\n        +void tick()\n        +void reset()\n        +Map~String,Tank~ getTanksCopy()\n        +List~Projectile~ getProjectilesCopy()\n        +ScoreBoard getScoreBoardCopy()\n        +Arena getArena()\n        +String winner()\n    }\n    class Main {\n        +static void main(String[] args)\n    }\n    GameEngine --> Arena\n    GameEngine --> ScoreBoard\n    GameEngine --> Tank\n    GameEngine --> Projectile\n    Arena --> ObstacleMap\n    Tank --> Position\n    Projectile --> Position\n    Orientation --> Tank\n    Orientation --> Projectile",
    "Program call flow": "sequenceDiagram\n    participant R as Main (runtime)\n    participant A as Arena\n    participant OM as ObstacleMap\n    participant T as Tank\n    participant GE as GameEngine\n    R->>OM: ObstacleMap.empty(); add(Position)\n    R->>A: new Arena(width,height,obstacles)\n    R->>T: new Tank(id, pos, orient, health) x2\n    R->>GE: new GameEngine(Arena, List<Tank>)\n    R->>GE: enqueue(tankId, Command)\n    R->>GE: tick()\n    GE->>GE: process commands (lexicographic ids, live only)\n    GE->>GE: spawn projectiles for FIRE (if in bounds, not obstacle)\n    GE->>GE: advance projectiles; detect collisions; update ScoreBoard\n    R->>GE: getTanksCopy(); getProjectilesCopy(); getScoreBoardCopy()\n    R-->>R: print one concise snapshot and exit",
    "Domain Mapping": [
        [
            "pom.xml: Java 11 compiler settings, junit-jupiter test dependency (scope test), and JUnit 5-capable Maven Surefire plugin configuration. Ensure mvn -q test runs tests.",
            "pom.xml",
