        ],
        [
            "Orientation.java: Enum with NORTH(0,-1), EAST(1,0), SOUTH(0,1), WEST(-1,0). Provide dx(), dy(), left(), right().",
            "src/main/java/Orientation.java",
            "domain-entity"
        ],
        [
            "Command.java: Enum with exactly MOVE_FORWARD, TURN_LEFT, TURN_RIGHT, FIRE.",
            "src/main/java/Command.java",
            "domain-entity"
        ],
        [
            "Tank.java: Validate nonblank id, non-null position/orientation; permit health==0, reject health<0. Mutable fields private Position position; private Orientation orientation; private int health;. Expose getters and isAlive(). Package-private: setPosition(Position), rotateLeft(), rotateRight(), applyDamage(int). Provide copy() that supports dead tanks.",
            "src/main/java/Tank.java",
            "domain-entity"
        ],
        [
            "Projectile.java: Fields shooterId, private Position position;, Orientation. Expose getters. Package-private void setPosition(Position). Provide copy(). No other mutators.",
            "src/main/java/Projectile.java",
            "domain-entity"
        ],
        [
            "ObstacleMap.java: Backed by a Set<Position>. Provide static empty(), add(Position), isBlocked(Position), and deep copy().",
            "src/main/java/ObstacleMap.java",
            "domain-entity"
        ],
        [
            "Arena.java: Validate positive width/height. Defensively copy obstacles. Provide inBounds(Position), isObstacle(Position), copy().",
            "src/main/java/Arena.java",
            "domain-entity"
        ],
        [
            "ScoreBoard.java: Initialize hits/kills=0 for provided ids. addHit/addKill increment; getHits/getKills/getScore (hits + 5*kills). Expose asMap() snapshot and copy(). Provide void reset(Collection<String> tankIds) to reinitialize to zero for given ids; GameEngine must call scoreBoard.reset(initialTanks.keySet()).",
            "src/main/java/ScoreBoard.java",
            "domain-entity"
        ],
        [
            "GameEngine.java: Own fields literally: private Arena arena; private final Arena initialArena; private Map<String,Tank> tanks; private final Map<String,Tank> initialTanks; private final ScoreBoard scoreBoard;. Constructor validates: at least 2 alive tanks with unique ids, distinct in-bounds, non-obstacle cells. Deep-copy arena and create empty FIFO queues per tank. Copy each supplied tank twice using exactly: Tank initialCopy = tank.copy(); Tank currentCopy = tank.copy(); this.initialTanks.put(tank.getId(), initialCopy); this.tanks.put(tank.getId(), currentCopy);. Enqueue adds to per-tank queue. tick(): for live tanks in lexicographic id order, process at most one command: MOVE_FORWARD attempts one cell unless out-of-bounds/obstacle/occupied by live tank; TURN_* rotates; FIRE spawns projectile in forward cell only if in bounds and not obstacle. Then advance all projectiles one cell using Projectile.setPosition; remove on out-of-bounds/obstacle; on first non-owner live tank at that cell, applyDamage(1), scoreBoard.addHit(shooterId), and addKill only if health==0; consume projectile on hit. reset(): this.arena = initialArena.copy(); this.tanks = new HashMap<>(); iterate initialTanks.values() (no streams) to copy into current tanks; recreate empty queues; clear projectiles; scoreBoard.reset(initialTanks.keySet()). getTanksCopy(), getProjectilesCopy(), getScoreBoardCopy() return fresh defensive copies. winner(): return sole surviving id only if exactly one alive among at-least-two-initial tanks; otherwise null. No Java streams anywhere.",
            "src/main/java/GameEngine.java",
            "orchestration"
        ],
        [
            "Main.java: Thin demo. Create small arena, tanks, engine; enqueue one or two commands; tick; print single concise snapshot of tank ids and scores; no loops, no System.exit. Use fully qualified java.util.Arrays.asList(...).",
            "src/main/java/Main.java",
            "environment-dependent"
        ],
        [
            "MainTest.java: Exactly three JUnit 5 tests. (1) Smoke: Main.main returns normally. (2) Blocked move + turn + reset fixture with Arena(6,5) and obstacle at (2,2); Alice at (1,2) EAST health3; Bob at (4,2) WEST health3; verify Alice does not move into obstacle, TURN_RIGHT changes to SOUTH, reset restores EAST and health3; verify zero score and no projectiles. (3) Hit/kill fixture with empty Arena(6,5); Alice at (1,2) EAST health3; Bob at (3,2) WEST health1; enqueue Alice FIRE; tick; verify Bob health0, Alice hits1/kills1/score6, no projectiles, winner is Alice. Always fetch fresh copies via engine.getTanksCopy() after each tick/reset; never inspect constructor-supplied Tank objects.",
            "src/test/java/MainTest.java",
            "automated-test"
        ]
    ],
